      critics: 'Critics warn that taking mindfulness out of its ethical and religious setting can oversimplify it, and that early claims about meditation’s benefits were often overstated.',
      history: [[-450, 'The Buddha teaches the Four Noble Truths in northern India'], [-250, 'The Abhidharma texts systematise Buddhist analysis of the mind'], [1979, 'Jon Kabat-Zinn adapts mindfulness meditation for a hospital stress clinic'], [2000, 'Scientists begin brain-imaging studies of experienced meditators']],
      thinkers: [['Siddhartha Gautama (the Buddha)', 'c. 5th century BCE', 'Taught that understanding the mind ends suffering', 'Teachings recorded in the Pali Canon'], ['Buddhaghosa', '5th century', 'Wrote the classic manual of meditation and mental states', 'Visuddhimagga (Path of Purification)'], ['Thich Nhat Hanh', '1926–2022', 'Brought mindfulness practice to the West', 'The Miracle of Mindfulness']],
